# Lyrical Project Rules

Lyrical is an anonymous poetry mobile platform built with Flutter and Supabase.

## Core Identity

- Users authenticate with a private email and password.
- Every user receives a randomly generated anonymous display name.
- The anonymous display name consists of a positive adjective plus an object, animal, or natural element.
- The anonymous display name must be unique and immutable.
- A user may edit only their gender, biography, and avatar.
- Never expose a user's email in public profile queries or UI.

## Technology

- Flutter with null safety.
- Supabase Auth, PostgreSQL Database, Storage, and Row Level Security.
- flutter_riverpod for state management.
- go_router for navigation.
- Feature-first project structure.
- Repository pattern for Supabase access.
- Material 3.
- Spanish is the default UI language.
- Code identifiers and comments must be in English.

## Architecture

- UI widgets must not call Supabase directly.
- Screens communicate with Riverpod providers.
- Providers communicate with repositories.
- Repositories contain Supabase queries.
- Reusable UI must be placed in `core/widgets` or feature widgets.
- Avoid unnecessary abstraction and overengineering.
- Keep files focused and reasonably small.

## Security

- Never place a Supabase service_role key in the Flutter application.
- Use only the publishable/anon client key in Flutter.
- All exposed database tables must use Row Level Security.
- Never rely only on Flutter validation for authorization.
- A user may update or delete only their own allowed content.
- Poetry moderation status cannot be changed by a normal client user.
- Public users may read only approved, visible, and non-deleted poems.

## Poetry Rules

- New poems start with status `pending`.
- Valid moderation statuses are `pending`, `approved`, and `rejected`.
- Authors cannot edit a poem's title or content after submission.
- Authors may hide, unhide, or delete their own poems.
- Hidden status is separate from moderation status.
- Prefer soft deletion with `deleted_at`.

## Development Workflow

- Before making changes, inspect the existing repository.
- Explain briefly which files will be created or modified.
- Implement only the requested phase.
- Do not rewrite unrelated files.
- Preserve working functionality.
- Handle loading, empty, success, and error states.
- Avoid deprecated Flutter or Supabase APIs.
- Run `dart format` and `flutter analyze` after relevant changes.
- Report remaining warnings or errors honestly.
- Never invent database columns that are not defined in the project schema.
